    "html": "<span class=\"kicker\">Act 1: Concepts &amp; Phases &middot; Execution Framework</span>\n  <h2>The Recursive Double Diamond within Every Phase</h2>\n  <p class=\"lede\">Rather than treating the British Design Council\u2019s Double Diamond as a static, multi-month project management waterfall, the Zip factory applies the <b>Double Diamond recursively within every single phase</b>.</p>\n  <div class=\"body scroll\">\n    \n    <div class=\"cols4\" style=\"margin-bottom:1.2em\">\n      <div class=\"card\" style=\"border-left-color:#3B82F6\">\n        <span class=\"pill int\" style=\"background:#1E3A8A;color:#93C5FD;border:none\">DIAMOND 1 \u00b7 DIVERGENT</span>\n        <h3 style=\"margin-top:.4em\">1. Discover</h3>\n        <p style=\"font-size:.82em\">Fan-out context gathering, legacy Azure monolith C# AST parsing, regulatory requirement retrieval, and edge-case discovery.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"card lime\" style=\"border-left-color:var(--zip-lime-dim)\">\n        <span class=\"pill good\" style=\"background:#283900;color:var(--zip-lime);border:none\">DIAMOND 1 \u00b7 CONVERGENT</span>\n        <h3 style=\"margin-top:.4em\">2. Define</h3>\n        <p style=\"font-size:.82em\">Synthesizing insights into rigid, machine-verifiable JSON Schema contracts (Artifacts A\u2013F). Establishing mathematical invariants.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"card\" style=\"border-left-color:#A855F7\">\n        <span class=\"pill int\" style=\"background:#4C1D95;color:#E9D5FF;border:none\">DIAMOND 2 \u00b7 DIVERGENT</span>\n        <h3 style=\"margin-top:.4em\">3. Develop</h3>\n        <p style=\"font-size:.82em\">Multi-agent parallel codegen; isolated zero-code-access test authoring; adversarial red-team probing in ephemeral sandboxes.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"card good\" style=\"border-left-color:#00D4FF\">\n        <span class=\"pill good\" style=\"background:#083344;color:#67E8F9;border:none\">DIAMOND 2 \u00b7 CONVERGENT</span>\n        <h3 style=\"margin-top:.4em\">4. Deliver</h3>\n        <p style=\"font-size:.82em\">Automated verification against non-negotiable exit gates; cent-for-cent ledger drift proof ($0.00); cryptographic sign-off.</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"callout lime\">\n      <b>The Compounding Advantage for Zip:</b> Skips neither discovery nor verification. Traditional LLM codegen jumps straight from vague prompt to code (skipping Diamond 1), resulting in massive rework. By enforcing convergence before code generation, requirements are mathematically proven unambiguous before any code is generated.\n    </div>\n\n    <div style=\"margin-top:.8em;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n      <span style=\"font-size:.82em;color:var(--muted)\">Every phase renders an interactive Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) in the Explorer.</span>\n      <button class=\"btn\" onclick=\"openExplorerSection('pipeline')\" style=\"font-size:.82em;padding:.4em .8em\">\n        \ud83d\udd78\ufe0f Open Phases Execution DAG in Explorer &rarr;\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  </div>"
